<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Askold and Dir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 882</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Askold, Dir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Askold and Dir were rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> in the 9th century, described in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varangians">Varangians</a> who took the city from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a>' tributaries and led a raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 860. According to the chronicle, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oleg-of-novgorod">Oleg of Novgorod</a> lured them out of the city in 882 and killed them, making Kiev his capital and so founding the united state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/askold-and-dir.jpg" alt="Askold and Dir" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Askold_of_Kiev.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
